      "text": "To find the maximum value of the expression \n\n\\[\n\\frac{x^4}{x^8 + 2x^6 - 4x^4 + 8x^2 + 16},\n\\]\n\nwe will first let \\( y = x^2 \\). This substitution simplifies the expression into a polynomial in terms of \\( y \\):\n\n\"\"\"\n\\[\ny^2 + 2y - 4y^2 + 8y + 16 = -3y^2 + 10y + 16.\n\"\"\"\n.\"\"\" \n\"\"\"\n\nAlright, now we have \n\\\\[\n-3y^2 + 10y + 16.\n\n\\\\boxed{3}\n\"\"\"\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of \\(\\frac{x^4}{x^8 + 2x^6 - 4x^4 + 8x^2 + 16}\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
